 stopped on decision CAT-03-01. This time there is no `## needs-human` section, so the run doesn't stop.\n\n- **Decision applied:** CAT-03-01 was answered with option 2, \"correct the shop\", and the plan cites it. The story stays adopted as written, and the title fix belongs to `not-found-title`. That fix is now in the working tree: `404.cshtml` no longer sets a title, so the page falls back to \"domaincentric.commerce\".\n- **Adopt mode:** nothing is built and no existing test changes. For each of the four scenarios the plan names the file and line where the behaviour lives and which test covers it:\n  - **The happy path** (`unknown-product-shows-the-not-found-page`) is fully covered by the browser test `NotFoundTitleE2eTest`.\n  - **`not-found-page-has-the-shop-title`** is covered by the same browser test, but no integration-level test checks it.\n  - **The two link scenarios** are only partly covered. The test checks each link's label and target but never follows the link to see the catalogue or home page open.\n- **Findings:**\n  - The story names the `product` context, but the not-found page is rendered by the web host, which belongs to no context. `/products/no-such-product` never reaches the Product context because the product route only accepts a GUID.\n  - CAT-03 can only really be adopted once `not-found-title` is committed. It is still running, and its change and its browser test aren't committed yet.\n\nI ran no other stage and changed no code or tests.","ttft_ms":2426,"type":"result","duration_ms":67800,"uuid":"af8fd818-4e0f-4b39-a0cc-bea27508a7fd","ttft_stream_ms":1697,"time_to_request_ms":62,"first_content_frame_ms":1698,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
